>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `mk_tactic_solver`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver : string * tactic -> TraverseExt.ssolver
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Turns a tactic into a named extension solver. `mk_tactic_solver (name, tac)`
proves `c` by solving `(map concl context_thms, c)` with `tac`, using the
untagged theorem context supplied by the simplifier.

### Failure

Construction never fails. Solving raises `HOL_ERR` if the tactic fails or
leaves subgoals.

### Example

``` hol4
>> val arith : TraverseExt.ssolver =
     simpExtLib.mk_tactic_solver ("arith", DECIDE_TAC);
>> #solve arith {stack = [], context_thms = [], recurse = REFL}
     “x < x + 1”;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver),
[`simpExtLib.add_safe_solver`](#simpExtLib.add_safe_solver).
